                    "text": "The VA\u2019s decision to terminate union contracts aligns with prioritizing veterans over bureaucratic bloat. Federal unions spent 750,000 taxpayer-funded hours on union activities in 2024\u2014time that should\u2019ve gone to veterans\u2019 care. Protecting underperforming employees and blocking accountability isn\u2019t \u201cjustice\u201d\u2014it\u2019s how D.C. robs taxpayers to fund union bosses.\n\nThe executive order restores focus: veterans first, not union politics. If AFGE spent half that energy fighting for vets instead of their own power, maybe the VA wouldn\u2019t be a disaster.",
